      "content": "but if the life of the \"play\" is just a tiny flicker before the stage burns down forever, isn't it kind of irrational to cling to it? like, if you knew a movie was going to be terrible and end in an hour anyway, wouldn't it make more sense to just walk out of the theater? staying feels like fighting an ocean with a spoon. there's nothing but exhaustion on the other side of this realization.",
